    "body": "Hello,\r\nI have added a customized continuation prompt in my starship fork. \r\n\r\nMy implementation created --continuation as a new flag for `starship prompt` to return the customized continuation prompt.\r\n\r\nAs for the configuration files, I added a field called `continuation_format` that is separate from the normal `format` field. I also added a field called `continuation_symbol` in the character module to customize the symbol used. The default has been left as a bold yellow arrow.\r\n\r\nI have only implemented this for bash and zsh so far. I do not have much experience with PowerShell, so I am currently finishing that implementation now. As for the other shells (fish, ion, elvish, etc.) do not seem to have continuation prompts. I have not done too much research into these other shells though, so I may be wrong for some of them.\r\n\r\nThis will be my first pull request for an open source project, so please let me know if my implementation should be altered in any way. I plan on creating a section in the documentation for the new fields I added to the configuration before I create my pull request. Also, please let me know if I am missing anything.",
