    "body": "In my recent commit, I added a call to `Set-PSReadLineOption -ContinuationPrompt` in the powershell profile, using a utf8 string as an argument. Now, when the continuation prompt is printed, the cursor is offset to the right by 11 characters.\r\n\r\nAny character typed in will be printed in the correct place, but the cursor is still offset. This offset is fixed in the next input line. This does not occur in the normal prompt, even though it is also utf8 encoded. It also does not occur if the continuation prompt is not a utf8 string.\r\n\r\nI am very unfamiliar with powershell, could anyone with more powershell experience see if there are any noticeable problems in the powershell profile script from my recent commit?",
