    "body": "https://github.com/raccog/starship/commit/2bb9998cdc04d0b37d92a5fe2ddf6280801952f0#diff-e4d3433fbae660101c14de3072af45910d7ed61e1dd144231dd1b07bd1a5fcaaR110 those are global variables that have quite a lot of side effects and the code takes explicit care not to modify them. (For example `[System.Console]::OutputEncoding` will also change the console code page which will effect any program started from PowerShell, possibly breaking it if it tries to print any OEM code page chars.\r\n\r\nGenerally the included `Invoke-Native` sets it to interpret the output of the executable as UTF-8 which will get decoded into a PowerShell/.NET `String`, you can check that string to see if it was decoded correctly.\r\n\r\nThere is also the possibilty that you have stumbled into a bug in PSReadLine when you set the continuation prompt from the prompt function, but that's just a guess and I haven't tried to verify this yet.",
