    "updated_at": "2021-12-12T14:25:56Z",
    "body": "I have version 5.1 of PowerShell and version 2.0 of PSReadLine.\r\n\r\nI think you are right that the prompt gets mangled on output. I can pass a Unicode string to `echo` and have it print the correct encoding even if `[System.Console]::OutputEncoding` is set to ASCII.\r\n\r\n`Set-PSReadLineOption` will output Unicode if you change `[System.Console]::OutputEncoding` to Unicode after the profile script initially runs. Then it will output a question mark again when `[System.Console]::OutputEncoding` is set to ASCII. So I think the prompt is being stored correctly when `Set-PSReadLineOption` is called, but interpreted incorrectly sometime during the output to console.\r\n\r\nI'm going to update PowerShell and PSReadLine and see if that fixes the problem.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
